{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-23T23:30:57.293Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"Each line narrows the results or prepares them for checking:\n\n- `colnames(annot)[1] <- \"probe\"` gives the annotation key the same name as the key in `results`, so the merge can match them.\n- `merge(..., by = \"probe\", all.x = TRUE)` joins symbols onto the results. `all.x = TRUE` keeps every results row, including probes with no annotation; their symbol will be `NA`.\n- The `annotated` filter keeps rows with a symbol that is present and not empty. This removes both missing annotations and the empty symbol.\n- The `sig` filter keeps rows whose adjusted p-value is below 0.05. Adjusted p-values account for testing many probes.\n- `direction` labels positive `logFC` as `\"up\"` and zero or negative `logFC` as `\"down\"`.\n- Sorting by adjusted p-value puts the strongest evidence first. Then `!duplicated(sig$symbol)` keeps the first (lowest adjusted p-value) probe for each symbol.\n- Setting row names to `NULL` makes the printed row numbers simple.\n- The last two commands show how many rows remain at each stage, print the selected probes, and count them by direction.\n\nWith unique probe IDs in `annot`, and assuming its nine rows match nine results probes, `merged` has 10 rows and `annotated` has 8: one result probe is unannotated and one annotation has an empty symbol. Duplicate **symbols** do not add rows to the merge; repeated **probe IDs** in `annot` can. The exact `sig` and `best` counts need the actual p-values and symbol mappings.","date":"2026-11-23T23:33:31.550Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I/.In-Class_CodingWithAI_I.ipynb.sage-chat","acp_log_key":"d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe:eb725e24-83cf-4fd8-bb3e-79516c9d76a5","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe.eb725e24-83cf-4fd8-bb3e-79516c9d76a5","acp_started_at_ms":1795476658590,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"eb725e24-83cf-4fd8-bb3e-79516c9d76a5","thread_id":"d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe","parent_message_id":"c8e593de-a9b3-40f2-8adc-cd5c7d2b27a2","acp_thread_id":"01a20abf-aee7-7720-95aa-ad6599a89875","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":12308,"cached_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1078,"reasoning_output_tokens":730,"total_tokens":13386,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T00:59:22.676Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"```r\n# Use the same column name so the probe IDs can be matched.\ncolnames(annot)[1] <- \"probe\"\n\n# Keep every result, including probes with no annotation.\nmerged <- merge(results, annot, by = \"probe\", all.x = TRUE)\n\n# Keep probes that have a usable gene symbol.\nannotated <- merged[!is.na(merged$symbol) & merged$symbol != \"\", ]\n\n# Keep results that pass the adjusted p-value cutoff.\nsig <- annotated[annotated$adj.P.Val < 0.05, ]\n\n# Label each significant result by the sign of its fold change.\nsig$direction <- ifelse(sig$logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")\n\n# Put the strongest adjusted p-values first.\nsig <- sig[order(sig$adj.P.Val), ]\n\n# Keep the top-ranked probe for each gene symbol.\nbest <- sig[!duplicated(sig$symbol), ]\n\n# Reset row names so they match the rows in this smaller table.\nrownames(best) <- NULL\n\n# Check how many rows remain after each filtering step.\nnrow(merged); nrow(annotated); nrow(sig); nrow(best)\n\n# View the selected probe for each gene.\nbest\n\n# Count selected genes by direction.\ntable(best$direction)\n```","date":"2026-11-24T00:59:31.721Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I/.In-Class_CodingWithAI_I.ipynb.sage-chat","acp_log_key":"d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe:343496b5-8d7e-45bb-8714-f425e0ad6187","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe.343496b5-8d7e-45bb-8714-f425e0ad6187","acp_started_at_ms":1795481963534,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"343496b5-8d7e-45bb-8714-f425e0ad6187","thread_id":"d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe","parent_message_id":"e23baee3-8859-489f-b07e-c2de86f41b9c","acp_thread_id":"01a20abf-aee7-7720-95aa-ad6599a89875","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":16317,"cached_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":517,"reasoning_output_tokens":245,"total_tokens":16834,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T01:01:11.273Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"The initial `arrange(probe)` preserves the base `merge()` order when adjusted p-values tie. Converting to a data frame at the end helps `all.equal()` compare it with `best`.\n\n```r\nlibrary(tidyverse)\n\nbest_tidy <- results %>%\n  # Join symbols while keeping every result row.\n  left_join(annot %>% rename(probe = probe_id), by = \"probe\") %>%\n  # Match the probe order from base merge().\n  arrange(probe) %>%\n  # Keep probes with a usable symbol.\n  filter(!is.na(symbol), symbol != \"\") %>%\n  # Keep statistically significant results.\n  filter(adj.P.Val < 0.05) %>%\n  # Label the direction of each fold change.\n  mutate(direction = if_else(logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")) %>%\n  # Put the most significant probes first.\n  arrange(adj.P.Val) %>%\n  # Keep the top-ranked probe for each symbol.\n  distinct(symbol, .keep_all = TRUE) %>%\n  # Make the output's table class match best for comparison.\n  as.data.frame()\n\n# Check that the columns and rows match best.\nall.equal(best, best_tidy)\n```","date":"2026-11-24T01:01:30.745Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I/.In-Class_CodingWithAI_I.ipynb.sage-chat","acp_log_key":"d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe:8342a120-cc8b-423c-a727-8481289a686c","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe.8342a120-cc8b-423c-a727-8481289a686c","acp_started_at_ms":1795482071602,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"8342a120-cc8b-423c-a727-8481289a686c","thread_id":"d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe","parent_message_id":"812134b4-327c-438f-b393-5c429055d9cd","acp_thread_id":"01a20abf-aee7-7720-95aa-ad6599a89875","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":19723,"cached_input_tokens":16314,"output_tokens":2248,"reasoning_output_tokens":1982,"total_tokens":21971,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T03:19:42.987Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"- Choose the probe with the highest average expression; its signal may be easier to measure reliably.\n- Choose the probe with the most variation across samples; it may better distinguish changes between samples.\n\nThese require expression measurements for each probe, which aren’t in the `results` table shown.","date":"2026-11-24T03:19:49.727Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I/.In-Class_CodingWithAI_I.ipynb.sage-chat","acp_log_key":"d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe:9d1b7512-a4a9-40f5-b905-1ee1279df783","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe.9d1b7512-a4a9-40f5-b905-1ee1279df783","acp_started_at_ms":1795490383740,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"9d1b7512-a4a9-40f5-b905-1ee1279df783","thread_id":"d0ff339b-3064-4afd-b527-f66f01e031fe","parent_message_id":"6f674280-af48-401e-b2ad-bbca8035479a","acp_thread_id":"01a20abf-aee7-7720-95aa-ad6599a89875","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":24782,"cached_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":321,"reasoning_output_tokens":258,"total_tokens":25103,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T04:26:33.594Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"Each line moves from probe-level results toward one significant row per gene symbol:\n\n- `colnames(annot)[1] <- \"probe\"` gives the annotation key the same name as the key in `results`, so `merge()` can match them.\n- `merge(..., by = \"probe\", all.x = TRUE)` attaches symbols to the results. `all.x = TRUE` keeps every results row, even when a probe has no annotation; its annotation fields will be `NA`. If a probe appears more than once in `annot`, its results row can appear more than once after the merge.\n- `!is.na(merged$symbol) & merged$symbol != \"\"` keeps rows with a real, non-empty symbol. This removes both missing annotations and the empty symbol.\n- `adj.P.Val < 0.05` keeps results that pass the adjusted p-value cutoff, which accounts for testing many probes.\n- `ifelse(sig$logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")` labels positive fold changes “up” and zero or negative changes “down.”\n- `order(sig$adj.P.Val)` sorts the significant rows from smallest adjusted p-value to largest, so the strongest statistical evidence comes first.\n- `!duplicated(sig$symbol)` keeps the first row for each symbol. Because of the sort, that is the row with the smallest adjusted p-value for that symbol; other probes with the same symbol are dropped.\n- `rownames(best) <- NULL` resets the row labels after filtering, for cleaner display.\n- The `nrow()` calls show how many rows remain after each stage. `best` prints the final table, and `table(best$direction)` counts its “up” and “down” rows.\n\nThe exact counts depend on which probes match and which p-values pass the cutoff. Also, the final table keeps the most significant **probe** per symbol; it does not combine results across probes.","date":"2026-11-24T04:26:44.420Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I/.In-Class_CodingWithAI_I.ipynb.sage-chat","acp_log_key":"bdc2ae98-71ca-4cf1-b58d-6106d3d01304:358ae9dc-ee03-42d8-95a8-5a22cbd387ca","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.bdc2ae98-71ca-4cf1-b58d-6106d3d01304.358ae9dc-ee03-42d8-95a8-5a22cbd387ca","acp_started_at_ms":1795494393328,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"358ae9dc-ee03-42d8-95a8-5a22cbd387ca","thread_id":"bdc2ae98-71ca-4cf1-b58d-6106d3d01304","parent_message_id":"9c7252b9-203b-4e46-98b2-0c80098b7e49","acp_thread_id":"01a20bce-41c1-7021-bd5c-b14ec0c9547b","acp_usage":{"input_tokens":12311,"cached_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":743,"reasoning_output_tokens":342,"total_tokens":13054,"model_context_window":121600},"acp_manager_finished":true,"acp_active_descendant_thread_ids":[],"acp_active_descendant_agents":0,"acp_subagent_limit_exceeded":false,"acp_background_terminal_processes":0,"acp_ai_usage_may_continue":false}
{"event":"chat","sender_id":"gpt-6-luna","date":"2026-11-24T04:26:51.509Z","history":[{"author_id":"gpt-6-luna","content":"```r\n# Use the same key name in both tables so the probe annotations can be matched.\ncolnames(annot)[1] <- \"probe\"\n\n# Keep every result, including probes that have no annotation.\n# A probe with multiple annotation rows can appear more than once.\nmerged <- merge(results, annot, by = \"probe\", all.x = TRUE)\n\n# Keep rows with a gene symbol; remove missing and blank symbols.\nannotated <- merged[!is.na(merged$symbol) & merged$symbol != \"\", ]\n\n# Keep results that pass the adjusted p-value cutoff.\nsig <- annotated[annotated$adj.P.Val < 0.05, ]\n\n# Label positive fold changes as up; zero and negative values are down.\nsig$direction <- ifelse(sig$logFC > 0, \"up\", \"down\")\n\n# Put the smallest adjusted p-values first so they are kept for each symbol.\nsig <- sig[order(sig$adj.P.Val), ]\n\n# Keep one probe per symbol, using the first (most significant) row.\nbest <- sig[!duplicated(sig$symbol), ]\n\n# Reset row numbers to make the final table easier to read.\nrownames(best) <- NULL\n\n# Check how many rows remain at each filtering step.\nnrow(merged); nrow(annotated); nrow(sig); nrow(best)\n\n# View the final table.\nbest\n\n# Count the up and down results in the final table.\ntable(best$direction)\n```","date":"2026-11-24T04:26:56.293Z"}],"generating":false,"acp_log_store":"acp-log/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I/.In-Class_CodingWithAI_I.ipynb.sage-chat","acp_log_key":"bdc2ae98-71ca-4cf1-b58d-6106d3d01304:bc8fc151-816c-4346-afd1-cf90f1c37963","acp_log_subject":"project.e3d18cfc-e2eb-46b5-9a2e-8cb41df2e6b8.acp-log.bdc2ae98-71ca-4cf1-b58d-6106d3d01304.bc8fc151-816c-4346-afd1-cf90f1c37963","acp_started_at_ms":1795494411322,"acp_working_directory":"/home/user/39_Coding_with_AI-I","acp_account_id":"6b19db69-db29-4124-a317-7e98612efdde","acp_runtime_kind":"codex","message_id":"bc8fc151-816c-4346-afd1-cf90f1c37963","thread_id":"bdc2ae98-71ca-